      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2012 International Society of Travel Medicine.",
        "AbstractText": "We report an open-label study comparing tadalafil and acetazolamide (n\u2009=\u200924) versus acetazolamide (n\u2009=\u200927) for prevention of high-altitude illness (HAI) at Mt. Kilimanjaro. Tadalafil group had lower rates of severe HAI compared with controls (4% vs 26%, p\u2009=\u20090.03), mostly because of decreased high-altitude pulmonary edema rates (4% vs 22%, p\u2009=\u20090.06)."
      },
